@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Matter `QCC74x` Contact Sensor Example
+
+This example functions as a contact sensor uses a test Vendor ID (VID) and a
+Product ID (PID) of **0x8001**.
+
+Please refer to the following documents for more information
+
+-   [QCC74X - Getting Started](../../../docs/platforms/qualcomm/qcc74x/getting_started.md)
+-   [QCC74X - OTA upgrade](../../../docs/platforms/qualcomm/qcc74x/ota_upgrade.md)
+-   [QCC74X - Matter factory data generation](../../../docs/platforms/qualcomm/qcc74x/matter_factory_data.md)
+
+## Build CHIP Contact Sensor example
+
+- Wi-Fi
+
+```shell
+./scripts/build/build_examples.py --target qcc74x-qcc743dk-contact-sensor-wifi build
+```
+
+## Test with chip-tool
+
+### Commissioning over BLE
+
+-   Reset the board or factory reset the board
+
+-   Enter build out folder of chip-tool and running the following command to do
+    BLE commission
+
+    -   Wi-Fi
+
+        ```shell
+        ./out/linux-x64-chip-tool/chip-tool pairing ble-wifi <device_node_id> <wifi_ssid> <wifi_passwd> 20202021 3840
+        ```
+
+### Subscribe booleanstate of contact sensor
+
+-   Start chip-tool with interactive mode
+
+    ```shell
+    ./chip-tool interactive start
+    ```
+
+-   Subscribe boolean state under chip-tool interactive mode
+
+    ```shell
+    booleanstate subscribe state-value <min-interva> <max-interval> <deivce_node_id> 1
+    ```
+
+    -   `<min-interva>`, min interval to report to boolean state of contact
+        sensor
+    -   `<max-interva>`, max interval to report to boolean state of contact
+        sensor
+    -   `<deivce_node_id>`, node id of contact sensor
+
+-   Click `Boot` button which will toggle boolean state and report its state to chip-tool
+
+
+## Actions on Boot Button
+
+- Pressed period between 100 ms and 1000 ms
+  - Toggle boolean state
+
+- Pressed period over 3000 ms
+  - Do factory reset
